# Conventions

> Progressive-disclosure reference for coding and process conventions.

## Code style
- Follow the configured linter and formatter for the primary language.
- Type hints / type annotations on all public interfaces.
- Keep functions small and focused; prefer existing utilities over new ones.

## Git / process
- Commit messages: imperative mood, concise summary line.
- Prefer Git worktrees for parallel agent work that may touch overlapping files.
- All changes to `.agents/` instruction and memory files are reviewed.

## Documentation
- Root `AGENTS.md` stays concise (< 150 lines) and imperative.
- Detail lives in `.agents/references/` and is loaded on demand.
